remoteClasses.doc:
Publishes audio and video from a Kurento media pipeline to a Media over QUIC (MoQ) relay.
<p>
  Create this endpoint with the relay <code>url</code> and the unique
  <code>broadcast</code> name under which to publish. Connect a media source
  (for example, a <code>WebRtcEndpoint</code>) to this endpoint, then call
  <code>publish()</code> to start the broadcast. Call <code>unpublish()</code>
  to stop it. MoQ subscribers, including
  <code>MoqSubscriberEndpoint</code> instances, can receive the broadcast.
</p>
<p>
  The endpoint encodes video as H.264 and audio as AAC and publishes them using
  the <code>moqsink</code> element from the
  <a href='https://github.com/moq-dev/moq'>moq-gst</a> GStreamer plugin. The
  plugin and the GStreamer H.264/AAC encoders must be installed on the Kurento
  Media Server host.
</p>
<h2>Usage</h2>
<pre><code>
  // JavaScript (Kurento Client, callback API)
  pipeline.create('MoqPublisherEndpoint', {
    url: 'https://relay.example.com',
    broadcast: 'my-broadcast.hang'
  }, function(error, publisher) {
    if (error) return onError(error);
    webRtcEndpoint.connect(publisher, function(error) {
      if (error) return onError(error);
      publisher.publish(onError);
    });
  });
</code></pre>
